        <transport>hwbinder</transport>
        <fqname>@1.0::IOffloadConfig/default</fqname>
    </hal>
    <!-- android.hardware.tetheroffload.control was declared here, but no service binary
         for it is ever installed (only the passthrough .so libraries). hwservicemanager then
         retries ctl.interface_start once per second forever, which blocks netd and makes
         'dumpsys tethering' time out. Stock firmware only declares tetheroffload.config,
         which is a passive library and needs no binary. Offload is optional; tethering
         falls back to software forwarding.

         android.hardware.wifi.hostapd is deliberately NOT declared here.
         /vendor/bin/hw/hostapd is an AIDL service (aidl::...IHostapd) and,
         like android.hardware.wifi.supplicant, AIDL HALs register themselves
         without a VINTF entry. A previous hidl @1.0 declaration here was
         wrong and had to be removed; the SoftAP does not start from a missing
         or malformed VINTF entry. See the device tree rro_overlays for the
         SoftAP band/security settings. -->
<hal format="hidl">
